@*
    Audit Definition (migration 276 / 279) -- Phase 3.

    Screen key : `org-audit-definition`
    Group      : Audit Management
    Menu       : Audit Management -> Audit Definition

    The audit is the primary entity. This screen is ONE audit list plus
    one 3-tab page per audit:

        Audit list
          +-- New Definition ------> Definition Details / Scope / Question Set
          +-- 3 dots -> View ------> the same three tabs, for that audit

    All three tabs work against the same definition id, so scope and
    question sets attach to the audit rather than becoming free-standing
    records. The standalone Scope Builder and Question Sets list screens
    are removed from the menu by migration 279; their routes stay alive
    for existing deep links.

    Everything lives in Partials/_audit-definition-workspace.cshtml, which
    hosts the existing screens rather than reimplementing them.
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.PracticeScreen

<partial name="Partials/_audit-definition-workspace" model="Model" />
